{{also|daa|daA|dáa|daá|da̰ã|da'a|daa-|Appendix:Variations of "da"}}
==Norwegian Nynorsk==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|nn|da}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|nn}} {{m|non|þá}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|doː|lang=nn}} {{nn-pronu-note}}

====Adverb====
{{head|nn|adverb}}

# [[then]] (at that time)
#: ''Fyrst '''då''' kan me gjera noko med det.''
#:: We can't do anything about it until '''then'''.
# [[then]] (in that case)
#: '''''Då''' er eg redd det er lite me kan gjera.''
#:: '''Then''' I am afraid there is little we can do.

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|nn}} {{m|non|þá er}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|doː|lang=nn}} {{nn-pronu-note}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|nn|conjunction}}

# [[when]] (at a time in the past)
#: '''''Då''' morgonen kom, hadde vêret vorte betre.''
#:: '''When''' the morning came, the weather had gotten better.

===References===
* {{R:The Nynorsk Dictionary}}

----

==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|þa|þā}}, from {{inh|sv|non|þá}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*þan||then}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/doː/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|Sv-då.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

===Adverb===
{{sv-adv|-}}

# [[then]]; at that time
# [[then]]; in that case
# [[what about]], [[how about]]
#: ''Den där, '''då'''?''
#:: '''What about''' that one?

===Conjunction===
{{head|sv|conjunction}}

# [[when]]; at the same point in time as
#: ''Vi sov '''då''' branden började.''
#:: We were asleep '''when''' the fire started.
# [[since]], [[as]]; by background of the case being that (''dated'')
#: '''''Då''' inget tvivel tycks råda om hans skuld, beslutar jag härmed...''
#:: '''Since''' there seems to be no doubts about his guilt, I hereby decide...

====Derived terms====
* {{l|sv|hej då}}

====Usage notes====
* In the first use it is far more common to use {{m|sv|när}} than {{m|sv|då}}, which is very rare in spoken language.
* In the second use it is far more common to use {{m|sv|eftersom}}; {{m|sv|då}} may be perceived as archaic.